					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE\n\nIn this example we start with a Sine Oscillator and we check whether the output of the oscillator is greater than 0 (the oscillator runs from -1 to 1).\nWe want to send this to the If node, but If is one of the few nodes that exclusively works on event flow.\nSo, we place an On Change node to take care of the conversion.\n\nTry switching the position of the Greater and On Change node.. The whole patch will break and hopefully teach you why the On Change is after the Greater ;-) "
					}
				},
